# hAIvemind Agent Rules

This project follows universal coding agent rules defined in `AGENTS.md` at the repository root.

## Core Rules (Always Active)

1. **Explore before acting** — read the codebase before modifying it
2. **Plan before implementing** — break tasks into steps
3. **Verify your own work** — run tests, check errors after every change
4. **Small incremental changes** — one logical change per step
5. **Manage context** — stay focused, reference specific files
6. **Communicate clearly** — ask when ambiguous, explain when acting
7. **Write quality code** — follow existing conventions, handle errors
8. **Use structured workflows** — spec → plan → implement → test → commit
9. **Delegate and parallelize** — batch independent operations
10. **Avoid anti-patterns** — no kitchen sinks, no skipping failures

## hAIvemind-Specific Rules

- **Self-building system.** Every session IS hAIvemind developing itself.
- **Roadmap-driven.** All work from `docs/roadmap.md`. Check before starting.
- **ESM only.** No `require()`. 2-space indent. Single quotes.
- **Protocol-first.** New message types → `shared/protocol.js` before use.
- **Module boundaries.** Routes = HTTP, Services = logic, WS = real-time.
- **Test-first.** New features get tests. Run before committing.
- **Stats are concrete.** "1915 tests" not "comprehensive test suite".
- **README < 200 lines.** Cut something if adding something.

## Key Architecture

- `server/index.js` — thin wiring (<200 lines), no logic
- `server/routes/` — HTTP handlers
- `server/services/` — business logic (52 modules)
- `server/ws/` — WebSocket real-time
- `server/state.js` — shared state (no globals)
- `shared/protocol.js` — message type definitions
- `client/src/` — Vue 3 frontend
- `tests/` — Playwright tests (78 files)

## Multi-Agent Design (Rules 24-25)

hAIvemind orchestrates multiple AI agents. When working on orchestration code:
- Use typed schemas at every agent boundary
- Design for failure first — retry logic, circuit breakers
- Log intermediate state — what each agent received, decided, produced
- Error-proof tool interfaces — specific failure messages

See `AGENTS.md` for full rules with rationale.
